      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I hope it's not too late for me to put in my two cents here about this. \n\nInventory is something that's always been specific for every game and platform. Inventories per world, as discussed in another post, could end up being extremely specific. It would make sense for the layout of the inventory itself to be customizeable within each world as well.\n\nAdditionally, we really need to be able to limit what people can have in their inventories. We limit the poly count for avatars, but inventory items can be just as intense if not more than an avatar can. I recommend that items in inventories that are uploaded by users be submitted to a public rating system, much like the trusted system already is. This added with moderation to filter out plain BAD items, could seriously help the community from the bad apples who would want to disrupt normal game play.\n\nOn the other hand, we have private items as well. For the most part, they should undergo the same filters and rules as above. I'm not sure how to cross that bridge, so perhaps some ideas there would help.\n\nI think this is a process that requires a lot of forethought. I imagine items at some point will attain an amount of abilities, materials, parts, attributes, etc. This, because perhaps one item, such as a 'hammer' in one world could be see as the same item in a different world, say 'Thor's Hammer'. A normal hammer wouldn't have the same attributes that Thor's Hammer does, but a much more powerful hammer could. This gives way to the need of an attribute system and linking of items from one world to the next.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
